  "description": "BREAK THE LINE\nSome trails don't ask politely. DEVIANT was made for those—the ones that bite back, that demand you commit before you can see what's next, that punish hesitation and reward precision. Shaped by the long climbs, loose rock, and steep descents of our Rocky Mountain surroundings, it's a titanium trail hardtail that doesn't negotiate with the mountain.\nBuilt around the 140mm RockShox Pike and a 430mm chainstay, DEVIANT brings the same uncompromising component logic that defines the rest of the VOID lineup into the dirt. Its Grade 9 titanium frame soaks the chatter that would haunt a carbon hardtail for days, while a T47 bottom bracket, UDH dropouts, and a Chris King Inset i7 headset ensure the spec is as dialed as the rider behind it. A 66° head tube angle and steep 76° seat tube keep things honest on the climb and committed on the way down. SRAM AXS Transmission, 29 × 2.6\" tire clearance, and a 31.6mm dropper-ready seat tube ensure there's nothing left to wish for—and nowhere left to hide.",
